# Let the unbound NVIDIA GA107 (10de:25a2, hardware/m7400qc/profile.toml) power down
# (ARCHITECTURE §6.4).
#
# The PCI core creates every device with runtime PM forbidden (power/control=on), and
# without a driver nothing ever allows it. The NVIDIA driver's own udev rule acts only
# on ACTION=="bind", which never happens at M1 (apex-dgpu.conf keeps drivers off). With
# "auto", the PCI core leaves the unbound function in D0 but lets the root port above it
# runtime-suspend, which cuts the GPU's power (D3cold).
# Acceptance: runtime_suspended_time is at least 95 % of 10 minutes idle.
#
# ATTR{power/control} names the attribute relative to the device's sysfs directory, the
# same form NVIDIA documents for its runtime PM rule; TEST skips kernels without it.

ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEM=="pci", ATTR{vendor}=="0x10de", ATTR{device}=="0x25a2", \
  TEST=="power/control", ATTR{power/control}="auto"
